#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:911
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr "Questions e responsas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:916
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I played around with the default runlevel, and now my machine reboots all "
"the time. What can I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:922
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter <userinput>linux single</userinput> at the <acronym>LILO</acronym> "
"prompt, and press <keycap>Enter</keycap> to boot into single user mode. Edit "
"the file <filename>/etc/inittab</filename> and change to the default "
"runlevel to something sane. <literal>3</literal> should normally be safe."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:934
#, no-c-format
msgid "My Machine <quote>halts</quote> just after booting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:939
#, no-c-format
msgid "See Question 1, above."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:947
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I scheduled some services to be run in runlevel X using &ksysv;, so why "
"aren't they working?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:954
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you're using &SuSE; or Delix (DLD) distributions, you also have to edit a "
"distribution specific file in <filename class=\"directory\">/etc</filename>. "
"Please have a look at the manual of your distribution for details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:962
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The approach to starting services used by the above mentioned distributions "
"makes configuration of services easy for the proprietary configuration tools "
"these distributions provide, but it is unfortunately non-standard. The "
"&ksysv; authors plan to write a generic extension for this approach some "
"time in the future, but don't hold your breath."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:971
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you're using a different distribution, please check you have all the "
"config files needed by the service, and whether they are in the correct "
"locations. Some daemons for example <application>Apache</application>, "
"(<acronym>aka</acronym> <command>httpd</command>) just die silently if their "
"configuration files are missing or misconfigured."
msgstr ""

